{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/889121-hunters-hunted-style-hunters-in-wta","id":889121,"title":"Hunters Hunted style hunters in WTA.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-12T08:05:56-07:00","id":889121,"title":"Hunters Hunted style hunters in WTA.","content":"saw a reference in a old MET book, that some hunters, viewed themselves as the ultimate sports hunters and the garou as the most formidible beasts on the planet.<br /> <br /> <br /> Is their a reason these losers seem to have disappeared, id enjoy lampooning them myself.<br /> <br /> or seeing them degraded and brutally killed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T11:12:51-07:00","id":889250,"title":"","content":"&quot;Hey, you know what would be great? Trying to hunt perpetually angry superbeasts that can make our only advantages shut down! It'd be so awesome!&quot;<br /> <br /> Darwin Award recipients, the lot of them. You wouldn't even need to wait that long.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T11:26:37-07:00","id":889254,"title":"","content":"oh so they disappeared being fumigated from existence, That makes sense.<br /> <br /> still think it would make a good joke.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T12:45:57-07:00","id":889297,"title":"","content":"Well it's not like they go attack caerns or anything. Sure it's suicidal, but when you're a mortal+ going after a big target, you can take the time to choose your target, pick a location, and wait for the right moment--like when they're alone and you have silver. (Optionally when they're badly weakened and out of Rage and Gnosis.)<br /> <br /> I mean, really. If a Skindancer can take the pelts of a full five Garou, surely a Hunter can take one down with their stronger powers. They might not have the same information that a Kinfolk would have, and there's less (but still some!) chance of being able to do it through betrayal, but...yeah. Hunters are just one of many things that you don't want to have stalk you in the WoD.<br /> <br /> As for why they're gone, they seem kinda jarring I guess and they don't fit into stories well? They're not part of a bigger picture, and when you kill them, the story just...ends. And if they take down one of your pack members, then it wasn't for any reason, a life taken just for human greed, not even because of Wyrm taint!<br /> <br /> ...I guess maybe it does work if you play up the pointless loss angle and connect it with normal humans hunting wolves. Could make a nice parallel plot in a story that focuses on poachers or other senseless environmental destruction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2214-traveller","name":"Traveller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2214_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T14:05:49-07:00","id":889345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Traveller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/889121-hunters-hunted-style-hunters-in-wta?p=889297#post889297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">surely a Hunter can take one down with their stronger powers</div> </div> </div> </div>Hunters Hunted are mortals, who at best might have Numina. You might be confusing them with the Imbued, maybe? <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4221-mrvyngaard","name":"MrVyngaard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4221_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T14:30:36-07:00","id":889361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrVyngaard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/889121-hunters-hunted-style-hunters-in-wta?p=889345#post889345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hunters Hunted are mortals, who at best might have Numina. You might be confusing them with the Imbued, maybe?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>...probably, yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2214-traveller","name":"Traveller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2214_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T14:41:14-07:00","id":889365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrVyngaard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/889121-hunters-hunted-style-hunters-in-wta?p=889345#post889345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hunters Hunted are mortals, who at best might have Numina. You might be confusing them with the Imbued, maybe?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>And even Imbued are presented as splintering like rotten wood in fights against werewolves. DO NOT PURSUE GAROU!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T14:56:59-07:00","id":889376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/889121-hunters-hunted-style-hunters-in-wta?p=889250#post889250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Hey, you know what would be great? Trying to hunt perpetually angry superbeasts that can make our only advantages shut down! It'd be so awesome!&quot;<br /> <br /> Darwin Award recipients, the lot of them. You wouldn't even need to wait that long.</div> </div> </div> </div>shame the veil keeps this from being LITERALLY true, it would be kind of funny...<br /> <br /> oh well you can have a similar ceremony somewhere in the umbra...<br /> <br /> Possibly some club in the glasswalker or bonegnawer homeland, with some comedian.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T23:02:57-07:00","id":889681,"title":"","content":"At the same time, if you know you are hunting werewolves, having silver bullets at the ready is a good equalizer. Unsoakable aggravated damage is the worst kind.<br /> <br /> I really doubt macho jerks who are wannabe Kraven the Hunters will last long in such attempts. However, I can accept there are hunters who are willing to kill werewolves in an attempt to defend humanity from them. They'd need to have immense Willpower, a lot of lore at identifying werewolves, and perhaps some members with Numina, but I can see some groups pulling it off occasionally provided they act smart.<br /> <br /> The biggest obstacle is that while literary and cinematic werewolves are often lone wolves, in the game you'll likely be facing an entire pack. For a group of Hunters Hunted style humans killing one Garou is difficult enough. Running into an entire pack will not end well.<br /> <br /> I suspect most such hunts are probably against Lunatics and Ronin. They are the ones most likely to pierce the Veil, and the least likely to have companions who can help them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T23:13:29-07:00","id":889689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/889121-hunters-hunted-style-hunters-in-wta?p=889681#post889681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the same time, if you know you are hunting werewolves, having silver bullets at the ready is a good equalizer. Unsoakable aggravated damage is the worst kind.<br /> <br /> I really doubt macho jerks who are wannabe Kraven the Hunters will last long in such attempts. However, I can accept there are hunters who are willing to kill werewolves in an attempt to defend humanity from them. They'd need to have immense Willpower, a lot of lore at identifying werewolves, and perhaps some members with Numina, but I can see some groups pulling it off occasionally provided they act smart.<br /> <br /> The biggest obstacle is that while literary and cinematic werewolves are often lone wolves, in the game you'll likely be facing an entire pack. For a group of Hunters Hunted style humans killing one Garou is difficult enough. Running into an entire pack will not end well.<br /> <br /> I suspect most such hunts are probably against Lunatics and Ronin. They are the ones most likely to pierce the Veil, and the least likely to have companions who can help them.</div> </div> </div> </div>But, see, Jam Weapons is a first rank Gift, so...<br /> <br /> 'I've got a clear shot! This is happening - die wolf!'<br /> <br /> Click.<br /> <br /> &quot;Shit.&quot;<br /> <br /> Click. Click. Clickclickclick.<br /> <br /> &quot;But... it was working perfectly...&quot;<br /> <br /> (exit mauled to death by a werewolf)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T10:35:33-07:00","id":890006,"title":"","content":"Well, keep in mind that a knock-down, drag-out fight involving Garou is often won or lost by your initiative roll anyway. Getting the first action against a werewolf is vital--and if that first action is 7 dice of unsoakable agg (a decent semiauto rifle with silver bullets) from long range, from someone he didn't know was even looking for him, he's in for some hurt. If you can get two shots off before he reaches you (which is entirely possible if you're like...on a rooftop), and you don't miss, he's probably either down or crippled. At that point either 1) he frenzies and can't use gifts, so pray you get a third round, or 2) he doesn't frenzy but you have a chance in melee against -5 dice of wound penalties. He'll probably blow 2-3 rage just shifting and getting to you, so if you know your target's already been fighting, he might be drained by the time you're in melee.<br /> <br /> Big game hunters don't go hand-to-hand against a lion or a rhino, why do it against a werewolf? Silver vulnerability is an enormous disadvantage against a surprise attack with ranged weapons. Bring a buddy or two and if you get the drop on the wolf, it's not even remotely a fair fight. The only chance a lone Garou has there is good intel; knowing there's hunters after him and either finding them first or skipping town. (Well, that and the Veil, but not if those hunters are high WP.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2214-traveller","name":"Traveller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2214_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T12:32:15-07:00","id":890080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/889121-hunters-hunted-style-hunters-in-wta?p=889365#post889365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And even Imbued are presented as splintering like rotten wood in fights against werewolves. DO NOT PURSUE GAROU!</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on which imbued they are. Avengers with their smiting powers could go toe to toe doing out good amounts of aggravated damage.. Soaking it though is gonna be the kicker...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Traveller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/889121-hunters-hunted-style-hunters-in-wta?p=890006#post890006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, keep in mind that a knock-down, drag-out fight involving Garou is often won or lost by your initiative roll anyway. Getting the first action against a werewolf is vital--and if that first action is 7 dice of unsoakable agg (a decent semiauto rifle with silver bullets) from long range, from someone he didn't know was even looking for him, he's in for some hurt. If you can get two shots off before he reaches you (which is entirely possible if you're like...on a rooftop), and you don't miss, he's probably either down or crippled. At that point either 1) he frenzies and can't use gifts, so pray you get a third round, or 2) he doesn't frenzy but you have a chance in melee against -5 dice of wound penalties. He'll probably blow 2-3 rage just shifting and getting to you, so if you know your target's already been fighting, he might be drained by the time you're in melee.<br /> <br /> Big game hunters don't go hand-to-hand against a lion or a rhino, why do it against a werewolf? Silver vulnerability is an enormous disadvantage against a surprise attack with ranged weapons. Bring a buddy or two and if you get the drop on the wolf, it's not even remotely a fair fight. The only chance a lone Garou has there is good intel; knowing there's hunters after him and either finding them first or skipping town. (Well, that and the Veil, but not if those hunters are high WP.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Very true Traveller. A decent enough hunter wouldn't Give that Garou a chance to kick in gifts to defend themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T13:00:40-07:00","id":890112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/889121-hunters-hunted-style-hunters-in-wta?p=890080#post890080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Depends on which imbued they are. Avengers with their smiting powers could go toe to toe doing out good amounts of aggravated damage.. Soaking it though is gonna be the kicker...</div> </div> </div> </div>Good luck surviving against anyone with Spirit of the Fray.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T13:14:05-07:00","id":890122,"title":"","content":"Crosspost the deadliest supernatural warrior thread from last year for good measurement <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/837527-deadliest-supernatural-warrior-results-and-analysis\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/837527-deadliest-supernatural-warrior-results-and-analysis\"> Deadliest supernatural warrior: results and analysis - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/837527-deadliest-supernatural-warrior-results-and-analysis\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/837527-deadliest-supernatural-warrior-results-and-analysis </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> https://www.dropbox.com/s/sk02dyo8h8fgb5d/match_vamp_were.png?raw=1 Ok! Time for the results and post-match analysis. First of all, here are the full results, with </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash","name":"Crytash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T14:32:28-07:00","id":890176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/889121-hunters-hunted-style-hunters-in-wta?p=890080#post890080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Depends on which imbued they are. Avengers with their smiting powers could go toe to toe doing out good amounts of aggravated damage.. Soaking it though is gonna be the kicker...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I thought the imbued only did lethal...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T16:12:29-07:00","id":890222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/889121-hunters-hunted-style-hunters-in-wta?p=890176#post890176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought the imbued only did lethal...</div> </div> </div> </div>In what little crossover material there is, Werewolf tends to give them the benefit of the doubt since Hunter doesn't use aggravated damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T18:12:46-07:00","id":890307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/889121-hunters-hunted-style-hunters-in-wta?p=889689#post889689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, see, Jam Weapons is a first rank Gift, so...</div> </div> </div> </div>Gifts of course are useful. But it is a very incompetent Glass Walker who breaks the Veil so badly that humans catch on to him. Out of all the tribes, it shouldn't be the Glass Walkers who are attracting hunters. And if the Garou is not a Glass Walker, chances are they won't they have that particular Gift.<br /> <br /> I don't run hunter plots unless the PCs screw up. But if I do, I get all Van Helsing on their ass. There's the guy that knows a lot. He has a bunch of people with him - they don't act alone. If they hunt vampires, they don't do it at night. They plan intelligently. And they use whatever resources they can get their hands on - True Faith, Numina, Hedge Magic, whatever.<br /> <br /> In most games I've seen, if there are hunters, they aren't very smart ones. That's probably because the ST wants to be easy on the PCs. I never like that. I only bring them in if the PCs are really screwing things up so they have no one to blame but themselves. So in my game, of you use Jam Technology to cancel someone's gun, the other four guys still open up and blast him away.<br /> <br /> I'm talking your traditional Peter Cushing monster hunter here who is fighting on the side of the angels. I don't count Pentex teams or other kinds as hunters; they are goons the PCs are meant to enounter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T09:46:31-07:00","id":890625,"title":"","content":"yeah I agree with Black Fox, Hunters showing up in any game should happen because the PC's screwed up hard enough to trigger a hunter's contacts in the area to contact them about some monster running around. A Garou is probably one of the most dangerous beings a hunter can go after with their gifts, natural talents, spirit contacts, ect. If a hunter is intelligent( which they should be if they're still alive) then they will go at a Garou in ways that keep the range as high as possible.<br /> <br /> Most hunters if they realise they're going after a pack would probably choose one Garou to stalk and take the pack down one by one, or use a weapon that can hurt all of the pack like attaching a bomb to the van a pack might use to drive to the next battleground against the Wyrm or try to get a pack in an enclosed space and gas them. When you're hunting Garou, rule number one would probably be 'don't get spotted',so remote detonators and camera feeds are your friends. Once the Garou knows what you look like or has your scent, you're days are numbered as theurges send englings to search for you and Garou try to track you, unseen in the umbra.<br /> <br /> And in the case of Jam weapons, like Black fox said he can have his allies open fire, or in the case of a solo hunter, don't carry just ONE high-powered sniper rifle that uses silver bullets, have 3 or 4 in case one gets jammed, and other types of weapons with silver if the Garou gets closer and worse case scenario it's a hard to jam a hammer or axe (difficulty 10 I believe).<br /> <br /> a hunter should not just be a gang-banger with a stake or silver knife, or at least a hunter who's meant to be a challenge shouldn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T10:47:38-07:00","id":890649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/889121-hunters-hunted-style-hunters-in-wta?p=890625#post890625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And in the case of Jam weapons, like Black fox said he can have his allies open fire, or in the case of a solo hunter, don't carry just ONE high-powered sniper rifle that uses silver bullets, have 3 or 4 in case one gets jammed, and other types of weapons with silver if the Garou gets closer and worse case scenario it's a hard to jam a hammer or axe (difficulty 10 I believe).</div> </div> </div> </div>Only snag here is that Jam Weapons is an area effect gift. It takes out all the weapons in an area (ear shot) for a round per success (granted its vs will power so any hunter taking on shifters should have high wills, so I guess there's that.) Its Gremlins and Jam TECHNOLOGY that are go on an item by item basis and neither of these are rank 1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T10:57:07-07:00","id":890650,"title":"","content":"You dont think an innocent cub, being killer by some idiot who thinks hes a righteous champion of God, makes for a bittersweet tale of vengeance?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T11:05:11-07:00","id":890651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/889121-hunters-hunted-style-hunters-in-wta?p=890650#post890650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You dont think an innocent cub, being killer by some idiot who thinks hes a righteous champion of God, makes for a bittersweet tale of vengeance?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, he's a werewolf it's his lot to die in the service of Gaia. Would he be avenged? Yeah but the pack that does the deed would probably give zero shits about the conviction of the guy, hunters a hunter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T11:48:49-07:00","id":890684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/889121-hunters-hunted-style-hunters-in-wta?p=890307#post890307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gifts of course are useful. But it is a very incompetent Glass Walker who breaks the Veil so badly that humans catch on to him. Out of all the tribes, it shouldn't be the Glass Walkers who are attracting hunters. And if the Garou is not a Glass Walker, chances are they won't they have that particular Gift.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oops. Just saw that all homids have access to that gift. It's not a Glass Walker only gift. My bad.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T12:37:00-07:00","id":890714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/889121-hunters-hunted-style-hunters-in-wta?p=890649#post890649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Only snag here is that Jam Weapons is an area effect gift. It takes out all the weapons in an area (ear shot) for a round per success (granted its vs will power so any hunter taking on shifters should have high wills, so I guess there's that.) Its Gremlins and Jam TECHNOLOGY that are go on an item by item basis and neither of these are rank 1.</div> </div> </div> </div>Jam Technology is also area effect. Gremlins is the only thing goes on an item-by-item basis, because it can permanently destroy said items. It can be had by any experienced Ragabash.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T12:56:01-07:00","id":890732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/889121-hunters-hunted-style-hunters-in-wta?p=890714#post890714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Jam Technology is also area effect. Gremlins is the only thing goes on an item-by-item basis, because it can permanently destroy said items. It can be had by any experienced Ragabash.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oops, misread Jam Tech, skipped over the 50 ft radius deal....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T17:18:45-07:00","id":890874,"title":"","content":"oh sorry, forgot about the area of effect on Jam weapons, so carrying a duffel bag of sniper rifles isn't going to help you. Even if it doesn't though, you'd still probably be far enough away to take your shot and scramble to another sniping nest or get out of there before the pack of wicked angry Garou makes you regret your life choices. If this hypothetical Garou hunter knew what jam weapons was, they could probably make a pretty dangerous tactic of establishing several sniper nests he can move to quickly, though the Garou might just run out before the hunter could get the second or third shot off. Maybe keep the duffel bag if a Ragabash is in the pack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T17:33:58-07:00","id":890880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/889121-hunters-hunted-style-hunters-in-wta?p=890874#post890874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh sorry, forgot about the area of effect on Jam weapons, so carrying a duffel bag of sniper rifles isn't going to help you. Even if it doesn't though, you'd still probably be far enough away to take your shot and scramble to another sniping nest or get out of there before the pack of wicked angry Garou makes you regret your life choices. If this hypothetical Garou hunter knew what jam weapons was, they could probably make a pretty dangerous tactic of establishing several sniper nests he can move to quickly, though the Garou might just run out before the hunter could get the second or third shot off. Maybe keep the duffel bag if a Ragabash is in the pack.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or there's a lot of cover in the way. Especially if you're anywhere near a caern, since forests are supposed to be 2spooky4u in keeping with the gothic atmosphere and there's more untouched wilderness. Even in a city, you could get behind a building and disappear. Cover and decoys can often be had.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T18:22:33-07:00","id":890895,"title":"","content":"Yeah that's true <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> but like I said in my first post here, that's why camera feeds and remote detonators are a hunter's friend, preferably detonators attached to bombs with LOTS of silver shrapnel. You don't even have to do the usual bomb the caern idea, and have the hunter stalk the Garou pack for a long time and find out where the homids live. Suddenly our good ol' defender of Gaia is snuggling into the sheets and gets a RUDE awakening.<br /> <br /> And yeah the cover thing is a good point seeing as the sniper loses a lot of effectiveness once the pack realises he's there and move to cover. Perhaps that's when the Silver shrapnel bomb goes off,if the hunter planned on the Garou where going to be there and lured them somehow. It might not kill them all, but there's are fair chance it will kill the Garou who just got a silver round put in them.","signature":