shrapnel bomb goes off,if the hunter planned on the Garou where going to be there and lured them somehow. It might not kill them all, but there's are fair chance it will kill the Garou who just got a silver round put in them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only thing I can think of is that you've read the Cyberpunk 2020 core one too many times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T06:35:26-07:00","id":891120,"title":"","content":"There is absolutely no way that a hunter survives that long without extensiv knowledge of werewolf culture, their habits and the packs goals as well as capabilities. I am a fan of making NPCs that would be playable and quite frankly i would struggle big time with playing a hunter that has the connection to all the other hunters, because they would go ham on me for hunting werewolves and not Vampires. <br /> <br /> Not only would they talk about the immense problems encountering Werewolves, but they would hit home their arguments with the argument that you would waste a perfectly capable Hunter or maybe even a complete group. Hunting Vampires might be dangerous, but you have tons of advantages against them.<br /> <br /> Hunting a Werewolf is just plain stupid, especially as they hunt Vampires too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash","name":"Crytash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name"